    },
    "body": "PR #1314's raw ranking counter counted any read as a hit, causing the roadmap to prescribe a frozen-ranker abstention fix. Its retained outputs instead show five correct reads out of 88 and five ranking errors among ten covered positions. This documentation change corrects that diagnosis, scopes the geometry/control/cost claims, and supplies a constructive DeepSeek handoff that can improve ranking, NoRead and bounded copy strength against predictive loss.\n\nThe mechanism synthesis connects 24 current and historical families to geometric attention: exact occurrence identity, contextual role/scope retention, scalar compatibility, directed H4/phase interpretation, shared dependent reads, and conditional routing/Hopf/S7/harmonic variants. The canonical plan, front-door READMEs, current state, evidence index and continuation instructions now follow that sequence. Original sealed outputs and historical reports are preserved with explicit corrections; no model is promoted.\n\nValidation: inspected the delivered source and retained outputs; independently verified retained manifest hashes and corrected count/provenance arithmetic; two independent reviews of the new audit/handoff and mathematical synthesis; `git diff --check`; claim-wording check; 792 local Markdown link targets resolve. This is source/research/document work: no Rust source edit, build, model forward, fit, model-ledger change or deletion. CI compatibility acknowledgements are not tests. Instrument defects remain an explicitly specified implementation task.\n\nReferences #973, #820, #1139, #962, #963, #964.\n",
